1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
“The mysterious unknown.”

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
are called...

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
What’s that?

14
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
-It's something Ging left with me.
-What?

15
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
He asked me to give this to you
when you became a Hunter.

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[Gon] So Dad left this for me?

17
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
REPLY X FROM X DAD

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
[narrator]
Three mysterious items were inside the box

19
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
that had been sealed with Nen...

20
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
One of these items, an old cassette tape,

21
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
gave Gon a long-awaited opportunity:

22
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
the chance to hear his father’s voice
for the first time.

23
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[Ging on tape] Hey... Gon.

24
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
So, you became a Hunter too, huh?

25
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
This is my dad’s voice...

26
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
[Ging] Anyway...

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
I have a question for you.

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Do you...

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
want to see me?

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[gasps]

31
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[Ging] If you do,

32
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
keep listening.

33
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:54,000
If you don’t,

34
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
just press the stop button.

35
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
I'm guessing that's a "yes".

36
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
But I’ll ask you one more time.

37
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Are you sure?

38
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Hunters are selfish creatures.

39
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
We’re willing to sacrifice
anything and everything

40
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
to get what we want.

41
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
If you just think
it would be nice to see me...

42
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
stop the tape here.

43
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
I’ll give you a minute.

44
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
What do you think?

45
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
[chuckles softly]

46
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
[bird squawks]

47
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
[tired exhale]

48
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[Ging sighs]

49
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
[Ging] You want to see me that much, huh?

50
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Well... I don’t want to see you.

51
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
[both gasp]

52
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
[Ging] Honestly, I don’t know
how I could face you.

53
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
After all...

54
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
I walked away from being a parent

55
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
for purely selfish reasons.

56
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
I’m not a decent guy...

57
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
[birds tweeting]

58
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
[Ging] I don’t have any way of knowing
how much time will pass

59
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
before you listen to this tape.

60
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
I figure it’ll be at least ten years.

61
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
But it doesn’t matter.

62
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
There’s one thing that will never change.

63
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
I’ll always be...

64
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
the guy I am.

65
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Bo!

66
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
[growls]

67
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[roaring]

68
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
[Ging] As you sit there,
listening to this tape,

69
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
I’m sure I’ll be off,
horsing around somewhere.

70
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
If you still want to see me,

71
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
find me.

72
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
But like I said...

73
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
I don’t want to see you.

74
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
If I hear you coming,

75
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
I’m gonna bolt.

76
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Catch me if you can.

77
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
You are a Hunter now, aren’t you?

78
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
[Killua] Hmm.

79
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
If you thought your dad
would be easy to track,

80
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
then you better think again.

81
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
-[Gon] Hey, wait.
-Hmm?

82
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
-Ging’s still there. Let it play.
-Oh.

83
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,000
[Ging] Oh...

84
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
there’s one more thing
I forgot to mention.

85
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
It’s... about your mother.

86
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,000
[gasps]

87
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
[Ging] If you want to know more,
keep listening.

88
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
If you don’t then--

89
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Are you sure?

90
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Uh-huh.

91
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
But what about the rest of it?

92
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
What if he left you another clue?

93
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
No way. Not him.

94
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
I can feel it.

95
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
And like I said before...

96
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
I do have a mom:

97
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Aunt Mito.

98
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
[Killua] I see.

99
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[grunts] Hey, are you hungry?

100
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I’ll go get us something to eat.

101
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
[Killua] Sure.

102
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
-Hey, Gon!
-Huh?

103
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
The tape started moving all by itself!

104
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Wait, what?!

105
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Is that aura?

106
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
It’s Nen!

107
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
And it’s rewinding the tape!

108
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Nen?

109
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
He’s close! He’s gotta be!

110
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
No. Over ten years ago
he imbued it with aura,

111
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
so it would start rewinding
the minute that it stopped!

112
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:34,000
But why?

113
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
I’ve no idea.

114
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Look! Now it’s recording!

115
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Wait, I think I get it.
He’s erasing his voice!

116
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
What?!

117
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
[Gon grunts]

118
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
It won’t stop, dammit!

119
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
[Killua] It’s still going!

120
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Even when I unplug it?

121
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
I’m breaking it.

122
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Sorry!

123
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Crap!

124
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
It’s no use.

125
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
The Nen’s protecting it!

126
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
[banging]

127
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
-[banging above]
-Huh?

128
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
[grunts]

129
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
It looks like it’s finished.

130
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[sighs]

131
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
[Killua] Look! Now it’s recording!

132
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Wait, I think I get it.
He’s erasing his voice!

133
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Gon] What?!

134
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[Gon trying to press button
on recording]

135
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
The duplicate cassette tape
was completely wiped, too.

136
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
I just don’t get why he would go through
all this trouble.

137
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
He probably didn’t want
to leave any clues or anything for us.

138
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
[Gon] What do you mean?

139
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
You can extract a whole lot of information
from a simple audio clip.

140
00:07:59,000 --> 00:07:59,000
[Gon] Really?

141
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
You can determine about
how tall the speaker likely is,

142
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
their weight, their age,

143
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
diseases, facial features,

144
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
even a psych profile.

145
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Oh...

146
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
From the noise in the background

147
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
you can even determine
their exact location.

148
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
But that’s not what he was worried about.

149
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
There’s something else.

150
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
What are you talking about?

151
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
His Nen abilities.

152
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[gasps]

153
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
There might be a Nen user somewhere

154
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
who can analyze data
better than a machine.

155
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
I bet there is.

156
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
They can hear your voice

157
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
and it would tell them everything
they’d ever need to know about you.

158
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
I see...

159
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Your dad is tough.

160
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Like, really tough.

161
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[grunts]

162
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
This is useless.

163
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Lucky it wasn’t the only clue.

164
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
We’ve still got two more left.

165
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
The ring and the memory card.

166
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,000
The ring probably won’t help,
but the memory card might.

167
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Yeah. But it’s smaller than a normal one.

168
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
You think we’re gonna need
special hardware for it?

169
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Wait-- You mean you can’t tell?

170
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
This is only designed to work with the JS.

171
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
What’s a JS?

172
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
A gaming console called the Joystation
from three generations back.

173
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Man, don’t you know anything?

174
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,000
If this island still has cassette players,

175
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
there’s gotta be an old console
around here somewhere.

176
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
There a toy store here?

177
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
I’m pretty sure there is.

178
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
-Okay. Hold on.
-Huh?

179
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Oh! Where are you going?

180
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
To the toy store.

181
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Huh?

182
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
-[Gon] It’s outside the port!
-Huh?

183
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
[Killua] Got it!

184
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Have a safe trip, okay?

185
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
[Gon] Oh... so this is a Joystation...

186
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
This takes me back.

187
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
I used to play it a lot.

188
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
There were a bunch of cult classics
made for it.

189
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Hmm...

190
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Then is this memory card a cult classic?

191
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
‘Cause I don’t see a title on it anywhere.

192
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
You’ve never played
any video games, have you?

193
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
That’s pretty weird.

194
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Seriously?

195
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
That’s not a game disc.

196
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
It holds a game's memory data.

197
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
I guess that means
we can’t use it to play.

198
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[Killua] Nope.

199
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
You’re supposed to put the disc in here.

200
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:28,000
But if you insert the memory card
and power it on without a game inside,

201
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
you can see all the different games

202
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
that are using that memory.

203
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Oh, okay.

204
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
[Killua] Huh...

205
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
It looks like there’s only one game
saved on it.

206
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
It’s called Greed Island.

207
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
[Gon] Greed Island?

208
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Well, anyway,
there are lots of saves on here.

209
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:52,000
It might be pointless
but I’ll try to copy the data.

210
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
[Joystation voice] Copying Greed Island.

211
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Okay.

212
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
[computer beeps]

213
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,000
What are you doing?

214
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Searching online.

215
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
We know what it’s called...

216
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
I’m looking for a store that sells it.

217
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,000
0 MATCHES

218
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
What? No way!
Not a single match?

219
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
That means it’s all sold out?

220
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
But I can’t find any used copies, either.

221
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Even a totally sold-out game
would be out there somewhere...

222
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Well... I guess it’s possible

223
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
this game was never actually
on the market.

224
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
What does that mean?

225
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Maybe it was an indie game or something

226
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
and it never got distribution.

227
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Or it could even be a game
that was banned from sale for some reason.

228
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
I’ll keep looking and see what I can find.

229
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Got it.

230
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Well, it turns out it was actually
sold through legitimate channels.

231
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
It says “Greed Island...

232
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,000
A hunting game exclusively...
for Hunters.”

233
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,000
For Hunters, huh?

234
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
What the--!
Look at that price tag!

235
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Five hundred and eighty million?!

236
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
-It’s five point eight billion!
-Say what?!

237
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
That’s crazy!

238
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
No game has ever cost that much money!

239
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Only a hundred copies were made.

240
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
That’s not very many, is it?

241
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
No, it’s practically nothing!

242
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Which means the developers
were really cocky!

243
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
But it makes sense.

244
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
The price tag is ridiculous,

245
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
unless, of course, you’re a Hunter.

246
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
That explains how they sold out.

247
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Do the developers have any more
left in stock?

248
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Good question.

249
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
I guess it’s worth a shot to ask them.

250
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[representative] I’m sorry,

251
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:30,000
the game you’re inquiring about
is no longer in stock.

252
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:34,000
And unfortunately, there are no plans
to re-release it at this time.

253
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Oh, okay. Thank you.

254
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
That was a dead end.

255
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Then... we’ll have to find someone
who has a copy

256
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
and see if they’ll let us have it.

257
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
You’re right.

258
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
So first we’re gonna need
to locate a seller.

259
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Why don’t we post an ad
on a reverse auction website.

260
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
But... where will we get the money?

261
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,000
We’ll pool our money from the Arena

262
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
and that gets us
to just over eight hundred million.

263
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
We still need another five billion.

264
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
-[Killua] Not necessarily.
-Huh?

265
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
With these private deals,
the seller has all the power.

266
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
And they usually set a higher price
than what they originally paid for it.

267
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
[Gon] Then... it’ll cost even more?

268
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Probably.

269
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,000
[both] Hmm...

270
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
[Gon] Well... we can still post a want ad,
just in case.

271
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Yeah. But I doubt anybody
is gonna click on it.

272
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
“We are looking for a game.

273
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Does anybody have
Greed Island for sale?

274
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Price... negotiable.”

275
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[both gasp]

276
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
[both] Oh!

277
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[gasps] Wow, look!

278
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
We already have more than 10,000 hits!
I don’t believe it!

279
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
I thought so.

280
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,000
It looks like they’re all trying
to unload counterfeit copies on us.

281
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Considering the high price,
we really should’ve seen this coming.

282
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
This isn’t gonna work.

283
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
No way we can verify
every one of these offers.

284
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Besides, what’s the point

285
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
if we can’t even tell
if it’s the real game?

286
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Then what do you think we should do now?

287
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Well, we need to uncover
a lot more information.

288
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Let’s dig deeper online.

289
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
But I’m really no expert
in all that stuff.

290
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
So, who do we know
who’s into gaming and the internet?

291
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
[gasps]

292
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
I... think I might know somebody...

293
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:25,000
[Gon] Huh?

294
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
In fact, he might even own
a copy of Greed Island already.

295
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Really? You think so?

296
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Guess I’ll ask him...

297
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
but I really don’t wanna.

298
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Who is it? Who is it?

299
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Hey. Gotoh? It’s Killua.

300
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Mister Gotoh?

301
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Yeah. Yeah, I’m doing great.

302
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Now? Who cares where I am?

303
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
If I tell you, Mom’s gonna find out
sooner or later.

304
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Anyway...
can you get Piggy for me?

305
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Who’s Piggy?

306
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,000
[pig grunts]

307
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[Milluki] What?!
Killua wants to talk to me?

308
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Screw that.
Tell him I stepped out or something.

309
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Shut up! You’re lying!

310
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
He hasn’t left the house in ages!

311
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
You go tell him if he doesn’t
pick up the phone in ten seconds,

312
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
I’ll break all of his figurines!

313
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
[irked grunt]

314
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
All right, all right.
Just put him on.

315
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Hey, Kil.

316
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,000
If you even think
about laying a finger on my collection,

317
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
I’m gonna kill you.

318
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Chill out, bro.
I was only kidding.

319
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
You’re so scary when you get mad!

320
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Wait, your brother?

321
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
What the hell do you want, anyway?

322
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Hurry up, I’m busy.

323
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Oh yeah. Greed Island?

324
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
I’ve heard of it.

325
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
It’s a super-rare game.

326
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Why? You’ve never been interested
in rare games.

327
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Do you own a copy?

328
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[Milluki] No, I don't.

329
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
-[sighs]
-[Milluki] I wanted one,

330
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,000
but I was five when it went on sale,
and I didn’t have any money.

331
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,000
But I heard there were
over twenty thousand requests

332
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
and only a hundred copies.

333
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Because of that each copy
costs a whole lot of Jenny;

334
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
about five point eight bil.

335
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:13,000
I tried to track one down
right after the thrill wore off,

336
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
but I couldn’t even find an owner.

337
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
It’s legendary for all kinds of reasons.

338
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
So, what’s the deal?

339
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
You looking for a copy or what?

340
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
-Kinda.
-[Milluki] Well, forget it!

341
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
It’s impossible.

342
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Even I had to give up.

343
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Oh? You had to admit defeat
‘cause it was too much for you to handle?

344
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
[annoyed growl]

345
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
That was years ago.

346
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
I’ve got a few leads now, smart guy.

347
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
But considering how much effort
it would take,

348
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,000
not to mention money,
it’s not worth my time.

349
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
So...

350
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
What were those leads
you were talking about?

351
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
[Milluki] Yeah, right.
Like I’d tell you for free.

352
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
If I had a Greed Island memory card,
would you... reconsider?

353
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[Milluki] Huh?

354
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
What are you saying?

355
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
[Killua] I just happened to get my hands
on a memory card, that’s all.

356
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
I figured with your skills,

357
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
you could analyze the data

358
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
and reverse engineer
the game itself, right?

359
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,000
[Milluki] Is that true?

360
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
You better not be lying.

361
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
[Killua] I never lie.

362
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Not when I’m making deals.

363
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
[Milluki] Okay, fine.

364
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
I have two leads.

365
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Wait a minute.

366
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Not over the phone!

367
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Don’t worry, Kil.

368
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,000
If somebody is eavesdropping,

369
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,000
this information won’t do them any good.

370
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Okay. First lead...

371
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Yeah. Yeah. I see.

372
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Okay, got it.

373
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
I’ll send it to you in the usual way.

374
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Sorry... but I kinda had to promise him
the copy of the memory card in exchange.

375
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Sure.
It’s just a copy anyway, so I don’t mind.

376
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Well in return,
I got two leads that sound pretty solid.

377
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,000
One’s a website.

378
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
It’s only accessible to Hunters,

379
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
which is no problem for you.

380
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,000
I’m almost positive we can find
more leads on Greed Island there.

381
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[Gon] Really?

382
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
That means
I get to use my Hunter’s License!

383
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Stupid!

384
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
If you use your home computer,
they’re gonna know your address!

385
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
You really want bad guys
showing up on this island

386
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
to steal your Hunter’s license?

387
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Oh. Yeah, I forgot.

388
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
You’ve gotta use public computers
for this kind of thing,

389
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
like at a hotel or a ‘net café.

390
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Well... there’s no rush.

391
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
I still don’t even know the address.

392
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Once my brother gets the memory card,

393
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
he said he’d send it to me.

394
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Or lead two:

395
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
The Yorknew City auction.

396
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
What?! Hold on, isn’t Yorknew City--?

397
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Yeah.

398
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
We’re supposed
to meet Kurapika and Leorio there.

399
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Also,

400
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
they’re holding the world’s greatest
auction there in September.

401
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,000
My brother said it’s probably a hoax,

402
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
but there’s a rumor going around

403
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,000
that someone’s gonna be auctioning off
dozens of copies.

404
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Then maybe... that someone is Ging!

405
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Yeah. So maybe it’s not a rumor.

406
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
It just might be credible!

407
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
[Gon] But we’re gonna need
a crazy amount of money to buy a copy.

408
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Yeah, you’re right about that.

409
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[Gon] I guess...

410
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,000
it really was our destiny
to go to Yorknew City.

411
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
[Milluki] Hmm...

412
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Battera, the tycoon,
is offering 17 billion for Greed Island

413
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:45,000
and 50 billion more for a memory card
with a complete saved game on it.

414
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
That's truly legendary.

415
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
[chuckles] Interesting...

416
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
I’ll put an end to this legend myself.

417
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
[Gon] Wow!

418
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
This is incredible!

419
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
What’s the big occasion?

420
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
You probably won’t be back to visit
for a little while.

421
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[gasps]

422
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Aunt Mito...

423
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Who knows
when you’ll get a chance to eat again?

424
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Better fill up while you can.

425
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,000
[chuckles softly]

426
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Mm-hmm.

427
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
[chuckles]

428
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,000
[Gon] All right!

429
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[Gon and Killua] Thank you for the food!

430
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
[indistinct chatter]

431
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
[Gon] Aunt Mito!

432
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
So long!

433
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
I’m gonna go find Ging, I promise!

434
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,000
And after I meet him,

435
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
I’m gonna come back to the island, okay?

436
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Bye! Take care! I’ll miss you!

437
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
[narrator] Ging told Gon to find him,

438
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:35,000
leaving a riddle behind
as a clue to his whereabouts.

439
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
In order to solve that riddle

440
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
and meet his father,

441
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Gon leaves home once again
with his friend, Killua, by his side,

442
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
and sets sail for Yorknew City.

443
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[theme song playing]

444
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[Gon] Coming up:

445
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

446
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

447
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

448
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

449
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Today, we're introducing Ging!

450
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
He’s my dad,
and I became a Hunter to find him!

451
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Oh, yeah, so what do you think
your dad wants, anyway?

452
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:14,000
I really don't know, but as soon as
I find him, I’ll be sure to ask!

453
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,000
[Gon] Next time:

454
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
"Wish x And x Promise"!

455
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Go to sleep or you’ll be late.

456
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Killua] Who, me? Nah. I don’t need sleep.

457
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Try to get plenty of rest, everyone!
